# Packages the uConsole needs that are not in Omarchy's lists, because Omarchy
# has never had to care about a Broadcom SoC.
#
# Installed by stage 20 alongside packages/base.packages.

# Vulkan on the CM5's VideoCore VII. Omarchy ships vulkan-intel, vulkan-radeon
# and vulkan-asahi; the Broadcom driver is the one that matters here, and
# without it anything Vulkan falls back to software rendering.
vulkan-broadcom

# Mesa's OpenGL for v3d. Normally pulled in as a dependency, listed explicitly
# so a change upstream cannot silently leave the desktop on llvmpipe.
mesa

# growpart, used by uconsole-firstboot-resize to grow root into the whole card.
# There is a parted fallback, but growpart handles the edge cases better.
cloud-guest-utils

# Diagnostics for the first-boot checklist in docs/05-first-boot.md.
mesa-utils
v4l-utils

# Firmware. NOT the `linux-firmware` meta-package: that pulls every vendor
# subpackage and put 1.0 GB in the image, of which ~840 MB was for hardware a
# CM5 cannot physically have - 387 MB of Intel, 152 MB of NVIDIA, 87 MB of
# AMDGPU, plus Atheros and MediaTek wifi. The same reasoning already excludes
# broadcom-wl and the NVIDIA/Intel driver stacks in packages/excluded.packages.
#
# Kept: broadcom (the CM5's own radio), whence (licence text), and three small
# ones that a USB peripheral might plausibly need - realtek covers most USB
# ethernet and wifi dongles, cirrus covers audio codecs.
linux-firmware-broadcom
linux-firmware-whence
linux-firmware-realtek
linux-firmware-cirrus
linux-firmware-other
